{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 3, :comments ["<b>ננתקה את מוסרותימו</b> — from the root מוסר." "<b>גם עבותימו</b> — thick ropes. The meaning is one in different words, for so is the way of eloquence, like: מה אקוב ומה אזעום (what shall I witness and what shall I rage)." "<b>יושב</b> — Because he mentioned יתיצבו מלכי ארץ (the kings of the earth set themselves), he said against them יושב בשמים (who sits in the heavens), that they are above over man. The Gaon [Saadia] said: the meaning of ישחק (He laughs) is that He makes them an object of laughter and mockery. The correct view is that HaShem created corporeal substance, which is the essence, and the forms, which are accidents — whatever a man makes or imagines are forms of living things. His name is exalted alone from being an essence, let alone an accident. But because the speaker is a man and so is the hearer, the Torah spoke in the language of the sons of man, so the hearer understands, and so they did: the earth is like the form of a man, and: ותפתח הארץ את פיה (and the earth opened its mouth), מירכתי ארץ (from the ends of the earth)." "<b>ולמו</b> — like להם." "<b>The word לעג</b> — always with the letter lamed, like ילעיגו לי (they mock me), therefore ואויבינו ילעגו למו (our enemies mock them), by way of pleonasm, as I will explain."], :book :psalms, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 2, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Psalms -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/tehilim"] ["Wikisource Mikraot Gedolot" "http://en.wikisource.org/wiki/Mikraot_Gedolot/"] ["Tanakh, Venice, 1617-1619" "https://dlib.rsl.ru/viewer/01007514045#?page=4"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:26:08.832129473Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}